<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antsiranana</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Diego Suarez</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antsiranana, formerly Diego Suarez, is a port city at the northern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, on one of the world's largest natural harbours. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> obtained it by the treaty of 1885 that ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-hova-war">Franco-Hova War</a> and made it a naval base. In 1942, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, British forces took it from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> France in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-madagascar">Battle of Madagascar</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antsiranana.jpg" alt="Antsiranana" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BelgianChocolate · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antsiranana_Diego_Suarez_typical_Arab-influenced_architecture_Madagascar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
